Done @BBuf — removed `test/registered/unit/managers/test_pp_proxy_record_stream.py` in [`b15b09e`](https://github.com/Phoenix3334/sglang/commit/b15b09e0fe3471238714e24718a6dcfc8439aa4d), as requested. The commit only deletes that 112-line mock test; the production lifetime fix and the existing fixture corrections are unchanged.

The PR body now reflects the removal and relies on the documented B300 experiments and existing PP integration results. The previous head `6745437` passed Base and AMD CI. [CI triggered by this cleanup](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41378151982) stopped at the 120-minute account cooldown before tests executed (earliest retry under the logged cooldown: 2026-11-02 04:18:01 UTC / 12:18:01 UTC+8).

@ShangmingCai, could you help with the code-owner review when available? The production PP fix is unchanged from the reviewed and GPU-tested version. Thanks!

